  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Back in the kitchen, Senya takes one look at sleepless Max and immediately guesses that Chef Barinov dragged him to a casino. Moments later, the Chef arrives and announces that he is moving out of Lyova's place and into Max's apartment.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Максимка всю ночь в казино играл.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Откуда вы всё это знаете?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Так это же известный этап.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Имей друга со здоровой почкой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да что ты такое несёшь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А он у Лёвы живёт ещё?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Сейчас начнётся этап большого новоселья.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Доброе утро, уважаемый Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "А ты почему ещё в форме?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Давай переодевайся, будем вещи перевозить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "А потом отметим наше новоселье.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Давай, парень, держись теперь крепче.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Максимка всю ночь в казино играл.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maximka was playing in a casino all night.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Maximka' before landing on 'played'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Откуда вы всё это знаете?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'How do you know all of that?' The meaning hinges on 'where from' working together with 'know' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Так это же известный этап.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Because that is a well-known stage.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'so' and 'this' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Имей друга со здоровой почкой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Have a friend with a healthy kidney.' Senya anchors the line on 'have', while 'kidney' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да что ты такое несёшь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What kind of nonsense are you talking?' Max addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'are carrying'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А он у Лёвы живёт ещё?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And is he still living at Lyova's place?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'and' and finishing on 'else'. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Сейчас начнётся этап большого новоселья.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now the big housewarming stage is going to begin.' Senya anchors the line on 'now', while 'housewarming' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Доброе утро, уважаемый Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good morning, respected Victor Petrovich.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'good' and finishing on 'esteemed'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "А ты почему ещё в форме?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And why are you still in your uniform?' Chef Barinov addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'uniform'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Давай переодевайся, будем вещи перевозить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Go change your clothes, we are moving my things.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'come on' before landing on 'to move'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "А потом отметим наше новоселье.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And afterwards we will celebrate our housewarming.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'then' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Давай, парень, держись теперь крепче.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Come on, pal, hang in there tight now.' Notice the reflexive suffix on the verb meaning 'hang in there', turning the action back on the subject. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
